When you need to create a Pull Request on the repo, follow this template for the description. Use the **exact section order** below. Generate a professional, concise description in **English** based on the code changes and user input.

### Why?
Explain the **motivation** (business value or technical fix). Use user input or infer from code logic.

_Replace me for a short overview of why this PR is being created._

### What?
Describe **what** is being modified at a high level (e.g. new table, new column, new logic).

_Replace me for a detailed explanation of what is being modified._
- _First changes;_
- _Second changes;_
- _..._

_How about some checkboxes?_
- [X] _First changes;_
- [ ] _Second changes;_
- _..._

### How everything was tested?
Describe the tests and environment. **Standard practice:** all tests should pass through **Forno** (staging); this is the default and encouraged flow. If the change did **not** go through Forno, provide a **justification** (e.g. scope, urgency, or exception approved by the team).

- **Table/SQL changes:** A simple **count**, **select** or statistics are sufficient.
- **New DAG:** A successful run on Forno is a good proof to display.
- **Other:** Add the information needed to show how well the change was tested.

_Please describe the tests you ran and any relevant details of your test configuration. If you did not run on Forno, explain why._

#### Screenshots
Reserve space or reference images for run result, dashboard, or sample query result when applicable.


### !Attention Points!
Call out what the reviewer should pay attention to or concerns after the merge (e.g. dependency order, backfill, breaking change, follow-up work).

_Replace me for what the reviewer will need to pay attention to in the PR or to cover any concerns after the merge._

### Checklist before opening the PR!
Use the **exact checklist** below. Leave items unchecked `[ ]` unless the user explicitly confirms they are done.

- [ ] My code follows the style guidelines and [name conventions](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mPPA716eoT3EZSqY0gA8a9ao4ObMyI9Y8QNd7CzlWWY) for DAGs, databases, columns, etc.
- [ ] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation;
- [ ] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works.
